                <pb facs="0764" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 25010/36.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Italian Chargé to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Italian Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Manchester,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-07-12"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">July 12, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 131.]</seg></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>: In continuation of
                    previous correspondence, I have the honor to transmit herewith to your
                    excellency a copy of the warrant of arrest issued June 13 last by the examining
                    magistrate of the civil and criminal court of Como against Mr. Porter
                    Charlton.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Montagliari.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
